      "writtenOn": "2025-12-03T19:22:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Currently `blink::SkiaImageDecoderBase::Decode` is implemented on top of `startIncrementalDecode` / `incrementalDecode`.  I think this is fine, but let me loop in Skia experts to double-check.\n\n@fmalita / @kjlubick: Can you please advise on the best path forward here?  Either:\n\n* Implement scanlines-based decoding (as in this CL).\n    - Pros: matches `SkBmpCodec` behavior and therefore makes `SkBmpRustCodec` a drop-in replacement\n    - Cons: will require having two separate implementations of `Decode` in Blink - e.g. `SkIncremetallyDecodingDecoderBase::Decode` and `SkScanlineDecodingDecoderBase::Decode`\n* Switch to incremental-decode-based decoding\n    - Pros:\n        - I vaguely recall that incremental decoding API is newer than (and maybe therefore preferred over) the scanline decoding API.  But I may be misremembering.\n        - Can reuse `blink::SkiaImageDecoderBase` as-is\n    - Cons:\n        - Would require reworking this CL\n        - `SkBmpRustCodec::onStartScanlineDecode` would return `kUnimplemented` (just using [the inherited/default implementation from `SkCodec`](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/skia/include/codec/SkCodec.h;l\u003d1063-1066;drc\u003ddde9a89a658e5b2ae75977e69dc5fc64ef240dac)) and therefore would behave differently from `SkBmpCodec`.",
